WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Welcome back and thanks for joining me today.&nbsp;
If we take a happy little zero-dimensional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:13.740
point and move it one unit to the right we get a&nbsp;
one-dimensional line. Move that line down by one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:22.440
unit and we get a big friendly two-dimensional&nbsp;
square. To get a 3D shape we want to move Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:29.520
Square one unit out of the board but we draw&nbsp;
that third dimension as a diagonal shift because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:38.520
we can't draw it perpendicular and we get a cube.&nbsp;
So a diagonal shift perpendicular to this one may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:44.520
send Mr. Cube to the fourth dimension. I've drawn&nbsp;
a cube diagonally shifted and I'm connecting up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:52.080
all the points to draw a 4D hypercube or at least&nbsp;
a drawing of one done by a 3D creature on a 2D&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:58.620
chalkboard. I might miss some lines but that's&nbsp;
okay, no mistakes in math just happy accidents.

